  "implementation": [
    "Private EventQuery carries dataset, ID, complete qualified scope, ordered explicit source bounds/topology and mandatory native snapshot; no FactRefs are required from the caller.",
    "One native transaction selects the exact-scope eligibility before shared payload; both references must be within the explicit cut. Empty/zero/omitted streams do not inherit records. Both full schema1 facts, canonical digests, body identity and original scope signature are verified.",
    "Exactly one logical reference per lookup; two independently valid alternatives refuse. Full hydration still selects by source identity without digest filtering, detecting conflicting source duplicates.",
    "The parent checks both returned source references, snapshot, event ID and signature; existing allocation/custody survives until the body drops. Same supervised private process carries bounded input/output, memory, deadline and cancellation.",
    "Existing exact-reference reads remain supported. No migration, persistent scientific encoding or advertised public capability changes."
  ],
